{"id":"word:hebrew:H3478","type":"word","title":"יִשְׂרָאֵל","subtitle":"H3478 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"he will rule as God ; Jisraël , a symbolical name of Jacob; also (typically) of his posterity","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יִשְׂרָאֵל (H3478) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 2507 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יִשְׂרָאֵל (Yisrâʼêl) means he will rule as God ; Jisraël , a symbolical name of Jacob; also (typically) of his posterity First listed occurrence: 1Chr 1 34."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יִשְׂרָאֵל","transliteration":"Yisrâʼêl","pronunciation":"yis-raw-ale'","strong":"H3478","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3478","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל","יִשְׂרָאֵֽל","יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל","יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל","יִשְׂרָאֵל֙"],"morphs":[["HNp",2260],["HR/Np",203],["HC/Np",33],["HC/R/Np",11]]},"definitions":{"short":"he will rule as God ; Jisraël , a symbolical name of Jacob; also (typically) of his posterity","usage":"Israel.","full":"H3478. Yisrael יִשְׂרָאֵל proper name and derivatives, see below I. שׂרה . יִשְׂרָאֵל 2507 proper name, masculine and of a people Israel ( El persisteth, persevereth (or jussive Let El persist ) [usually contendeth (Nes Eg.60 ff. ) or Let El contend (Gray Prop. N. 218 ), but see Dr Hast. DB JACOB 530 ]; on vocalization see Lag BN 131 f. Kit 1Chr 4:16 (Hpt); MI 5 , + 5 t. ישראל ; in Egyptian Y-si-r-'l Steind ZAW xvi (1896), 331 , compare Breasted Bib. World ix (1897), 62 ff. Paton Syr. and Pal. 134 ; Assyrian Sir-'-lai (= יִשְׂרְאֵלִי ) Schr KG 356 ff., 364 ; COT Gen 36:31 ; 1Kin 16:29 . &#8212; On a possibly relation of ׳יִשׂ to proper name שָׂרָה שָׂרַי, see RS K 257, 2nd ed. 34 ; — compare שְׂרָיָה(וּׅ ; — Ισραηλ : 1. proper name, masculine second name of Jacob Gen 32:29 28 t. Genesis (JE), Exod 32:13 (JE), Hosea 12:13 ; Judg 18:29 ; Exod 6:14 ; Num 1:20 ; 26:5 (all P), 2Kin 17:34 ; 1Chr 1:34 8 t. Chronicles, Psa 105:23 ; יִשׂ ׳בֵּית Ruth 4:11 ; יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי (literal) Gen 42:5 3 t. E, 2 t. P + Exod 1:7 (P; transition to wider use), 1Kin 18:31 ; 1Chr 2:1 +; = 12 tribes Exod 28:9 7 t. P; וְיִשׂ יִצְחָק אַבְרָהָם ׳אֱלֹהֵי 1Kin 18:36 ; 1Chr 29:18 ; 2Chr 30:6 . 2. proper name, of a people (usually masculine Judg 11:17 f. but feminine 1Sam 17:21 ; 2Sam 24:9 [not || 1Chr 21:5 ], compare Dr on the passage Albr ZAW xvi (1896), 57 f. ): name of Hebrew nation; usually derived from 1 , but ׳יִשׂ more common in early usage than יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי (see בֵּן p. 120:b): a. (1) undivided kingdom; ׳יִשׂ Gen 47:27 (J), 49:7 (poem in J) + 108 t. J E, Deut 1:1 ; 18:6 ; 33:10 (poem) + 76 t. D, Gen 34:7 ; Exod 12:15 42 t. P; Judg 5:2 , 7 (twice in verse) + 104 t. Judges; often 1and 2Samuel; 1 Kings 1-12; ׳כָּליִֿשׂ of whole people 2Sam 8:15 +, of whole army 11:1 +, opposed to Judah 2:9 + (so also later). (2) ׳יִשׂ = Northern tribes, distinguished from Judah, even before disruption, 2:9 , compare 2:10 ; 3:10 ; 4:1 ; 5:5 ; 12:7 ; 20:1 ; 1Kin 1:35 ; 4:20 ; 5:5 +; so at disruption 12:16 (3 t. in verse); 12:18-19 , then usually of Northern kingdom, till its fall, 12:28 ; 1Ki 24:7; 1Ki 24:10 + very often Kings, Amos 1:1 ; 2:6 ; 3:14 +, Hosea 1:5 ; 4:15 (twice in verse); 5:3 (twice in verse); 5:5 +, Micah 1:13 , etc. (3) ׳יִשׂ of Southern kingdom, Judah, rarely before fall of Samaria Isa 1:3 ; 8:18 ; Micah 1:14-15 , so יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי 1Kin 12:17 ; after fall of Samaria, ׳יִשׂ (less often יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי ) occurs of entire people, in reference to past or future 2Kin 21:8 ; 23:22 ; Isa 17:9 ; Psa 103:7 ; Jer 2:3 ; 50:17 , 19 +; ׳יִשׂ also = Judah 2:14 , 31 ; 4:1 +, Ezek 13:2 , 4 , 16 ; 14:1 , 7 , 9 +, Isa 40:27 ; 41:8 ; 42:24 +, Ezra 2:59 = Neh 7:61 ; Ezra 2:70 ; 3:11 +, Neh 10:34 ; 10:3 +, Psa 14:7 (twice in verse) = Psalm 53:7 (twice in verse), 147:2 ; 149:2 +, etc. (4) usage in Chronicles: ׳יִשׂ of whole people 1Chr 2:7 110t., of Northern kingdom 2Chr 11:1 16 t., of Judah 12:6 ; 19:8-9 t. (5) ׳יִשׂ personified as י ׳עֶבֶד , Isa 44:1 , 21 ; 49:3 . b. יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי , (1) of undivided people Exod 1:12 (J), 3:9 (E) + 72 t. J E, Deut 3:18 ; 10:6 25t. D, Genesis 32:33 327t. P; Judg 1:1 60t. Judges; seldom 1and 2Samuel, 1 Kings 1-12; in 1 Kings 13&#8212;2Kings 25 passive in reference to older history (rarely otherwise). (2) seldom of Northern kingdom Amos 2:11 9 t. Amos, Hosea; 2Chr 13:12 7 t. Chronicles. (3) of Judah (late) Ezek 2:3 ; Neh 1:6 (twice in verse); Ezra 3:1 ; Joel 4:16 +, 2Chr 31:5 . c. ׳יִשׂ בֵּית Exod 16:31 ; 40:38 142t. (see בַּיִת 5d ( δ ); 81 t. Ezekiel, where = Judah; see especially 37:16 ); יִשׂ בָֽתֵּי ׳שְׁנֵי Isa 8:14 . d. other phrases, see sub שֵׁבֶט עַם, עֵדָה, (יעד) מַטֶּה, (נטה) מֶלֶךְ, כִּסֵּא, הַר, גְּבוּל, בְּתוּלָה, בַּת, אֶרֶץ, אִישׁ, ; also (in epithet of ׳י ) below אֱלֹחִים אוֺר, אָבִיר, , I. מִקְוֶה מֶלֶךְ, גָּוֺאל, (I. קוה ), I. צוּר (V. צור ), קָדוֺשׁ , I. רָעָה 1d (3). e. ׳יִשׂ = the laity, opposed to priests, etc. (late): Ezra 10:25 ; Neh 11:3 ; 1Chr 9:2 ; ׳כָּליִֿשׂ Ezra 2:70 ; 10:5 ; יִשׂ ׳הָעָם 9:1 ; יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי Nehemiah 10:40, compare יִשׂ ׳שְׁאָר Neh 11:20 . יִשְׂרָאֵל proper name, of a people Israel (Biblical Hebrew id. , √ I. שָׂרָה ); — יִשׁ ׳אֱלַהּ Ezra 5:1 ; 6:14 ; 7:15 ; לְיִשׂ ׳מֶלֶךְ 5:11 ; יִשׂ ׳בְּנֵי 6:16 , יִשׂ ׳עַמָּא 7:13 .","rootNote":"from 8280 and 410 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 1 34","keyReferences":["1Chr 1 34","1Chr 1 43","1Chr 2 1","1Chr 2 7","1Chr 4 10","1Chr 5 1","1Chr 5 1","1Chr 5 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":2507,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 1 34","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יִשְׂרָאֵֽל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Np"},{"reference":"1Chr 1 43","book":"1Chr","chapter":1,"verse":43,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":1,"englishT